{"task_id": "HumanEval/8", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\n\n\ndef sum_product(numbers: List[int]) -> Tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\" For a given list of integers, return a tuple consisting of a sum and a product of all the integers in a list.\n    Empty sum should be equal to 0 and empty product should be equal to 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_sum = 0\n    current_product = 1\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        current_sum += num\n        current_product *= num\n\n    return (current_sum, current_product)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/8", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\n\ndef _calculate_sum(numbers: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of integers in a list.\n    Uses the built-in sum function for efficiency.\"\"\"\n    return sum(numbers)\n\ndef _calculate_product(numbers: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the product of integers in a list.\n    Iterates through the list to multiply elements.\"\"\"\n    product = 1\n    for number in numbers:\n        product *= number\n    return product\n\ndef _handle_empty_list() -> Tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Returns identity values (0 for sum, 1 for product) for an empty list.\"\"\"\n    return (0, 1)\n\ndef sum_product(numbers: List[int]) -> Tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\" For a given list of integers, return a tuple consisting of a sum and a product of all the integers in a list.\n    Empty sum should be equal to 0 and empty product should be equal to 1.\n    >>> sum_product([])\n    (0, 1)\n    >>> sum_product([1, 2, 3, 4])\n    (10, 24)\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return _handle_empty_list()\n    else:\n        total_sum = _calculate_sum(numbers)\n        total_product = _calculate_product(numbers)\n        return (total_sum, total_product)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/9", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef rolling_max(numbers: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"From a given list of integers, generate a list of rolling maximum element found until given moment\n    in the sequence. Records the maximum value seen from the beginning up to each current position.\"\"\"\n\n    if not numbers:\n        return []\n\n    rolling_maxes = []\n    current_max = float('-inf')\n\n    for number in numbers:\n        if number > current_max:\n            current_max = number\n        rolling_maxes.append(current_max)\n\n    return rolling_maxes"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/10", "solution": "```python\ndef is_palindrome(string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\" Test if given string is a palindrome.\n    It compares the string with its reversed version.\n    \"\"\"\n    return string == string[::-1]\n\n\ndef make_palindrome(string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\" Find the shortest palindrome that begins with a supplied string.\n    It identifies the longest palindromic suffix and prepends the reverse of the remaining prefix.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not string:\n        return \"\"\n\n    for i in range(len(string)):\n        suffix = string[i:]\n        if is_palindrome(suffix):\n            prefix = string[:i]\n            reversed_prefix = prefix[::-1]\n            return string + reversed_prefix\n```"}
