{"task_id": "HumanEval/31", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef is_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Check if a given number is prime. Returns True if n is prime, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n    if n < 2:\n        return False\n    if n == 2:\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n\n    limit = int(math.sqrt(n))\n    for i in range(3, limit + 1, 2):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return False\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/31", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef is_prime(n):\n    \"\"\"Determines if an integer is a prime number.\n    Uses an efficient O(\u221an) trial division algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 2:\n        return False\n    if n == 2:\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n\n    def _calculate_sqrt_limit(num):\n        \"\"\"Calculates the integer square root to define the trial division limit.\"\"\"\n        return math.isqrt(num)\n\n    def _check_divisibility(num):\n        \"\"\"Performs trial division by odd numbers up to the square root.\"\"\"\n        limit = _calculate_sqrt_limit(num)\n        for i in range(3, limit + 1, 2):\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    return _check_divisibility(n)\n```"}
