{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_third(l: list):\n    \"\"\"This function sorts elements at indices divisible by 3 while preserving others.\n    It returns a new list, leaving the original input list unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not l:\n        return []\n\n    extracted_elements = []\n    divisible_indices = []\n    for i, item in enumerate(l):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            extracted_elements.append(item)\n            divisible_indices.append(i)\n\n    sorted_extracted = sorted(extracted_elements)\n\n    result = list(l)\n\n    for i, sorted_val in zip(divisible_indices, sorted_extracted):\n        result[i] = sorted_val\n\n    return result\n```"}
