{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "def change_base(x: int, base: int):\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    return string representation after the conversion.\n    base numbers are less than 10.\n    >>> change_base(8, 3)\n    '22'\n    >>> change_base(8, 2)\n    '1000'\n    >>> change_base(7, 2)\n    '111'\n    \"\"\"\n    if x == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    is_negative = False\n    if x < 0:\n        is_negative = True\n        x = abs(x)\n\n    digits = []\n    while x > 0:\n        remainder = x % base\n        digits.append(str(remainder))\n        x //= base\n\n    result = \"\".join(digits[::-1])\n\n    if is_negative:\n        return \"-\" + result\n    else:\n        return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "```python\ndef _validate_base(base: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Validates the base parameter constraint.\n    Returns True if base is less than 10, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    return base < 10\n\ndef _convert_to_base(number: int, target_base: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Converts a decimal number to a specified target base.\n    Uses the standard division-remainder algorithm to build the string.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return '0'\n\n    digits = []\n    while number > 0:\n        remainder = number % target_base\n        digits.append(str(remainder))\n        number //= target_base\n\n    return \"\".join(reversed(digits))\n\ndef change_base(x: int, base: int):\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    Returns string representation after the conversion; base numbers are less than 10.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not _validate_base(base):\n        raise ValueError(\"Target base must be less than 10.\")\n\n    return _convert_to_base(x, base)\n```"}
