{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "```python\ndef fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the Fib4 sequence iteratively.\n    This function avoids recursion to efficiently calculate the sequence based on the sum of the four preceding elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the four preceding values for n=0, 1, 2, 3\n    # a = fib4(i-4), b = fib4(i-3), c = fib4(i-2), d = fib4(i-1)\n    a, b, c, d = 0, 0, 2, 0\n\n    # Iterate from the 4th element up to n\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib4 = a + b + c + d\n        a = b\n        b = c\n        c = d\n        d = next_fib4\n\n    return d\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "```python\ndef median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_list = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_list)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # Odd length: return middle element\n        return sorted_list[n // 2]\n    else:\n        # Even length: return average of two middle elements\n        mid1 = sorted_list[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_list[n // 2]\n        return (mid1 + mid2) / 2.0\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "```python\ndef fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    # Handle base cases\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # For n >= 4, use iterative approach with O(1) space complexity\n    # Initialize the four previous values: fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n    f_n_minus_4 = 0  # fib4(0)\n    f_n_minus_3 = 0  # fib4(1)\n    f_n_minus_2 = 2  # fib4(2)\n    f_n_minus_1 = 0  # fib4(3)\n\n    # Iteratively compute fib4(4) through fib4(n)\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        current_fib4 = f_n_minus_1 + f_n_minus_2 + f_n_minus_3 + f_n_minus_4\n        # Shift values for the next iteration\n        f_n_minus_4 = f_n_minus_3\n        f_n_minus_3 = f_n_minus_2\n        f_n_minus_2 = f_n_minus_1\n        f_n_minus_1 = current_fib4\n\n    return f_n_minus_1\n```"}
