{"task_id": "HumanEval/59", "solution": "```python\ndef largest_prime_factor(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return the largest prime factor of n. Assumes n > 1 and is not a prime.\"\"\"\n\n    def trial_division(num: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Finds all prime factors of a number using trial division.\"\"\"\n        factors = []\n        d = 2\n        temp_num = num\n\n        while d * d <= temp_num:\n            while temp_num % d == 0:\n                factors.append(d)\n                temp_num //= d\n            d += 1\n        if temp_num > 1:\n            factors.append(temp_num)\n        return factors\n\n    def find_prime_factors(num: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Orchestrates prime factorization using trial division.\"\"\"\n        return trial_division(num)\n\n    def get_largest_factor(factors: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Extracts the largest factor from a list of factors.\"\"\"\n        return max(factors)\n\n    prime_factors = find_prime_factors(n)\n    return get_largest_factor(prime_factors)\n```"}
