{"task_id": "HumanEval/73", "solution": "```python\ndef smallest_change(arr):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the minimum changes to make an array palindromic using a two-pointer approach.\n    This achieves O(n) time and O(1) space complexity.\"\"\"\n    if len(arr) <= 1:\n        return 0 # Empty or single-element arrays are already palindromic.\n\n    changes = 0\n    left = 0\n    right = len(arr) - 1\n\n    while left < right: # Compare symmetric elements from both ends of the array.\n        if arr[left] != arr[right]:\n            changes += 1\n        left += 1\n        right -= 1\n\n    return changes\n```"}
