{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "```python\ndef closest_integer(value):\n    \"\"\"\n    Orchestrates the string-to-integer conversion with away-from-zero rounding.\n    Handles input processing, distance determination, and applying specific rounding rules.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def validate_input(val: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates if the input string represents a number.\n        As per design, it trusts the input and does not raise exceptions.\n        \"\"\"\n        return True\n\n    def perform_conversion(val: str) -> float:\n        \"\"\"\n        Converts a validated string representation to its floating-point value.\n        \"\"\"\n        return float(val)\n\n    def determine_distance(val: float) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if the floating-point value is exactly equidistant (X.5) from two integers.\n        This uses `abs()` and checks the fractional part for equality with 0.5.\n        \"\"\"\n        abs_val = abs(val)\n        fractional_part = abs_val - int(abs_val)\n        return fractional_part == 0.5\n\n    def apply_away_from_zero_rule(val: float) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Applies the away-from-zero rounding rule for equidistant values (X.5).\n        Positive numbers are rounded up, negative numbers are rounded down.\n        \"\"\"\n        if val >= 0:\n            return int(val) + 1\n        else:\n            return int(val) - 1\n\n    # Input Processing Layer\n    _ = validate_input(value)\n    converted_value = perform_conversion(value)\n\n    # Calculation Layer\n    if determine_distance(converted_value):\n        # Apply away-from-zero rule for equidistant cases\n        result = apply_away_from_zero_rule(converted_value)\n    else:\n        # Apply standard rounding (round half away from zero also for non-equidistant cases)\n        if converted_value >= 0:\n            result = int(converted_value + 0.5)\n        else:\n            result = int(converted_value - 0.5)\n\n    # Output Layer\n    return result\n```"}
